WEBVTT

01:04.105 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:08.443
Chaos ensues
after the implementation

01:08.526 --> 01:10.236
of the new waste disposal policy.

01:10.737 --> 01:13.364
People are getting rid of things
they should not throw away

01:13.448 --> 01:15.742
out of fear that they may end up
having to pay fines.

01:15.825 --> 01:17.160
FROM YEONG-BEOM
TO GEUM-MYEONG

01:17.243 --> 01:19.162
I couldn't just throw it away.

01:19.245 --> 01:21.456
I had to pay for the garbage bags I used.

01:21.956 --> 01:23.666
I made sure to be respectful.

01:24.167 --> 01:26.836
Residents put warning signs
in front of their homes…

01:26.920 --> 01:30.715
Oh, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot.
Hey, hurry, hurry, hurry.

01:31.925 --> 01:33.676
Hot, hot, hot.

01:33.760 --> 01:35.178
WEDDING INVITATION

01:39.557 --> 01:42.435
I tore off the limbs
and cut up one of the big stuffies

01:42.519 --> 01:45.021
so the pieces would go
in the bags they need to.

01:45.772 --> 01:47.023
It all felt really wrong.

01:47.607 --> 01:48.858
You're out of kimchi too?

01:48.942 --> 01:50.860
Everyone knows I ended the engagement?

01:51.736 --> 01:53.363
Oh, what in the world do you eat?

01:54.447 --> 01:55.949
At least you're still alive.

01:56.032 --> 01:57.534
Life goes on for the living.

01:57.617 --> 02:00.954
Get off your rear end.
Your mom called me again.

02:02.455 --> 02:03.873
She wants to make sure you're okay.

02:04.582 --> 02:08.211
You heard of pain spots, huh?
Areas of the body that feel pain.

02:09.295 --> 02:11.297
There's pain spots in our organs.

02:12.841 --> 02:14.634
In all of our internal organs.

02:18.513 --> 02:20.557
Heartache isn't simply a thing you say.

02:21.182 --> 02:23.017
There's pain you actually feel

02:23.601 --> 02:24.686
where your heart is.

02:25.770 --> 02:26.896
Your heart

02:27.814 --> 02:32.694
feels… this tight pain.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.280
It's true.

02:35.363 --> 02:38.658
Call your family, you ungrateful child.

02:40.910 --> 02:44.372
I couldn't see
my best friend of seven years any longer,

02:45.456 --> 02:47.500
but my best friend of 20 years

02:48.835 --> 02:50.461
was still by my side.

02:51.379 --> 02:53.256
Geum-myeong, are you okay?

02:53.756 --> 02:56.885
You have food to eat?
You have nothing in your fridge, huh?

02:57.635 --> 02:59.220
Do you want me there?

02:59.304 --> 03:00.847
I made a lot of jangjorim.

03:01.723 --> 03:05.852
Even married couples can part ways.
High-class people do what they want.

03:06.561 --> 03:09.731
So, uh, he isn't calling you, right?

03:10.732 --> 03:13.026
Okay, okay. I won't mention that guy.

03:13.109 --> 03:14.736
Sure, good night.

03:18.364 --> 03:20.491
She always says, "Forget it." Forget what?

03:22.911 --> 03:24.037
She say that again?

03:25.622 --> 03:28.708
Well, she only ever says "Forget it,"
or "Mom, you don't have to know."

03:29.876 --> 03:31.628
I wish she'd talk to me

03:31.711 --> 03:33.421
or that she'd use me to vent.

03:33.504 --> 03:34.589
She's a grown-up now.

03:35.548 --> 03:37.425
What's a mother for otherwise?

03:38.134 --> 03:40.720
No one worries more about her than I do.

03:41.387 --> 03:44.015
Do you feel bad
she's not asking you for help anymore?

03:44.682 --> 03:47.018
She'd always ask me first.

03:47.936 --> 03:50.104
Now she tells her problems
to everyone else

03:50.605 --> 03:51.856
and turns me away.

03:52.357 --> 03:53.191
Traitor.

03:54.234 --> 03:56.069
There's no betrayal worse than that.

03:57.237 --> 03:59.489
You're the only one I'm telling, Mom.

04:01.032 --> 04:02.408
This is a secret,

04:03.409 --> 04:05.787
but I like Kim Jeong-geun.

04:07.372 --> 04:08.539
I might even marry him.

04:13.044 --> 04:14.087
Why?

04:14.170 --> 04:15.880
Why do you like Jeong-geun?

04:15.964 --> 04:18.883
He's cute.
The cutest boy in our neighborhood.

04:20.718 --> 04:21.844
Goodness.

04:23.721 --> 04:26.557
Geum-myeong, you're a big girl now. Huh?

04:27.058 --> 04:28.810
You have a crush on a boy.

04:31.646 --> 04:33.273
You know what though?

04:34.524 --> 04:38.444
I do wish
you'd mature a little more slowly.

04:38.945 --> 04:40.738
Just be a child longer.

04:40.822 --> 04:41.656
Why?

04:43.032 --> 04:44.993
Because you're adorable right now.

04:45.702 --> 04:47.036
You're so adorable now.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.333
Geum-myeong.

04:53.293 --> 04:57.547
You tell me all your secrets
when you get bigger, okay? Hmm?

04:57.630 --> 05:00.341
You're my secret keeper, Mom.
Of course I will.

05:00.425 --> 05:01.884
-Of course.
-Oh yeah?

05:01.968 --> 05:04.220
I'm closest to you, Mommy.

05:04.304 --> 05:05.930
Even more than Kim Jeong-geun?

05:07.140 --> 05:08.766
Goodness.

05:09.726 --> 05:12.437
Mom, who's your best friend?

05:12.520 --> 05:15.523
Who me? Oh, I think that'd be you.

05:16.524 --> 05:19.444
Do you……have a crush on anyone?

05:20.361 --> 05:23.364
Oh, my crush is Yang Gwan-sik.

05:24.073 --> 05:24.949
Over me?

05:25.033 --> 05:28.953
Well, no, you're my favorite
in the whole wide world.

05:29.037 --> 05:31.664
Good, because you're my favorite, Mom.

05:31.748 --> 05:32.874
Really?

05:32.957 --> 05:35.918
Yeah, that's why
I bought Popeye for a snack.

05:36.002 --> 05:39.922
Because you said once
Popeye was your favorite snack.

05:40.006 --> 05:41.591
Apollo is my favorite.

05:41.674 --> 05:42.675
Oh, dear.

05:42.759 --> 05:44.510
You got Popeye 'cause of that?

05:44.594 --> 05:47.430
I decided not to buy the Apollos this time

05:47.513 --> 05:49.766
because I love you so much, Mommy.

05:50.266 --> 05:52.393
Oh gosh.

05:52.477 --> 05:53.353
POPEYE

05:53.436 --> 05:54.645
Thank you.

05:55.146 --> 05:56.814
I'm very glad to hear that.

05:57.940 --> 05:59.734
We used to be
each other's world.

06:00.526 --> 06:04.072
One left that world behind
while the other stuck around.

06:04.155 --> 06:07.158
And what do you want for dinner?
Anything you like.

06:07.950 --> 06:09.077
I want jangjorim.

06:09.160 --> 06:10.703
I'll make you jangjorim for…

06:10.787 --> 06:13.748
My mom remained
the sweetest mother in the world,

06:13.831 --> 06:16.459
and she was always my secret keeper.

06:39.023 --> 06:41.317
What are we going to do
with all this food?

06:42.443 --> 06:44.237
-It's no fun just us two.
-Mm.

06:44.737 --> 06:47.949
She has an office job.
It's hard for her to get here on weekends.

06:48.449 --> 06:49.617
It'd be tiring for her.

06:50.993 --> 06:54.414
After the thousandth time
she called to ask if I had eaten,

06:55.289 --> 06:57.375
I started feeling really hungry.

06:59.710 --> 07:01.838
Mom, I'm hungry.

07:01.921 --> 07:03.965
I missed my mom's food.

07:04.632 --> 07:07.885
Hi, baby. You didn't say you were coming.

07:07.969 --> 07:09.137
I used vacation days.

07:10.513 --> 07:13.182
Ah, but why didn't you call me?
It's pretty late.

07:13.266 --> 07:14.308
I'm hungry, Mom.

07:14.892 --> 07:17.103
Yeah! We've got food. We do.

07:17.186 --> 07:19.772
I'll make steamed rice.
Just wait.

07:24.152 --> 07:24.986
Honey.

07:25.486 --> 07:27.989
I just made a whole pot of jangjorim.

07:28.072 --> 07:31.701
Your dad's been peeling quail eggs
to give to you since yesterday.

07:32.201 --> 07:36.706
Oh! Chonggak kimchi too.
I have well-fermented chonggak kimchi.

07:36.789 --> 07:38.791
You like it sour, right?

07:38.875 --> 07:42.545
Eun-myeong likes it fresh,
and you want it sour.

07:43.129 --> 07:46.382
I always have to keep them separate.
You guys always give me more to do.

07:46.466 --> 07:47.300
Goodness.

07:50.720 --> 07:52.638
The floor's cold. Wait. Here.

07:59.729 --> 08:02.190
The truth is, it was obvious.

08:02.732 --> 08:03.649
It was obvious

08:04.692 --> 08:07.612
how forlorn it was inside that apartment,

08:07.695 --> 08:11.574
just five minutes ago,
how lonely they must've felt.

08:12.241 --> 08:13.659
All right. All right.

08:15.786 --> 08:18.164
If you'd called me,
I would've come to the airport.

08:18.915 --> 08:21.292
Why, so you can wait there
an hour earlier?

08:31.761 --> 08:33.679
Eat and go back to sleep, okay?

08:34.180 --> 08:36.933
Oh my God. I'm not a pig in a cage.

08:38.559 --> 08:40.978
As a child,
when I fell, she gave me candy.

08:41.062 --> 08:41.896
Here.

08:42.396 --> 08:45.316
Oh, Mom,
you know broccoli's just the worst.

08:45.399 --> 08:47.193
It'll help you digest.

08:48.402 --> 08:49.320
I think

08:50.238 --> 08:53.241
we should have noodles
for a simple lunch. Here.

08:55.117 --> 08:56.869
This is a simple lunch?

08:57.954 --> 09:00.206
Then what would
a complicated one look like?

09:00.831 --> 09:02.667
After I recovered from the mumps,

09:02.750 --> 09:04.126
she made me pork cutlet.

09:04.210 --> 09:05.962
You love spicy noodles.

09:10.007 --> 09:10.841
Geum-myeong.

09:12.218 --> 09:13.886
Steamed bun, your favorite.

09:13.970 --> 09:15.263
You love red beans.

09:16.347 --> 09:18.891
They were eager
to do one more thing

09:18.975 --> 09:20.810
for their heartbroken daughter.

09:21.852 --> 09:23.312
Yeah.

09:24.021 --> 09:27.108
Yeah, well, she arrived out of the blue.

09:27.191 --> 09:30.653
She missed her mother,
that's why.

09:31.362 --> 09:32.280
Yes, son.

09:40.580 --> 09:41.831
Amberjack.

09:41.914 --> 09:44.292
Look what I got. Real amberjack.

09:45.209 --> 09:46.711
Is there fake amberjack?

09:47.211 --> 09:49.672
They took care of me yet again.

09:50.381 --> 09:52.800
Dad, I'm going to gain weight.

09:52.883 --> 09:54.385
Whoa, amberjack. Great!

09:55.303 --> 09:58.389
They made sure
that I didn't lose a single pound.

10:00.141 --> 10:01.100
Really?

10:01.601 --> 10:02.810
Yeah, sure.

10:03.894 --> 10:07.064
-Oh, it's so cold.
-Hey. Your brother wants to say hi.

10:08.608 --> 10:10.901
What?

10:10.985 --> 10:13.362
You miss me
now that you're a soldier, huh?

10:13.446 --> 10:16.240
"Oh, Geum-myeong."

10:16.324 --> 10:18.909
You got dumped, huh?
He dumped you, right?

10:18.993 --> 10:20.911
"Oh, Yeong-beom."

10:23.706 --> 10:27.335
In that refuge, where I was
comfortable but also uncomfortable,

10:27.835 --> 10:31.964
I hibernated like a bear in the winter
to regain my strength.

10:46.270 --> 10:47.104
Geum-myeong.

10:48.648 --> 10:49.774
Geum-myeong.

10:51.734 --> 10:52.568
Geum-myeong.

10:53.402 --> 10:54.487
Huh? What?

10:56.489 --> 10:57.782
Wanna sleep longer?

11:00.451 --> 11:02.370
Uh, are you tired?

11:02.453 --> 11:04.538
Yeah.

11:05.915 --> 11:07.083
Come on, get up.

11:07.708 --> 11:09.794
I wanna sleep longer.

11:10.294 --> 11:12.338
Come, let's go somewhere together.

11:12.421 --> 11:14.173
Can we just go later?

11:18.386 --> 11:21.472
Ah, Dad! I'm tired!

11:24.892 --> 11:26.435
Okay, go back to sleep.

11:42.743 --> 11:45.663
I'll never know why
I realized it at that moment.

11:53.629 --> 11:55.881
When I went on trips with Yeong-beom,

11:55.965 --> 11:57.967
I'd happily wake up at 4:00 a.m.

12:01.554 --> 12:03.973
You knew I'd come out, right?

12:46.640 --> 12:48.434
Why do I have a life jacket on?

12:59.862 --> 13:03.699
GEUMEUNDONG

13:07.369 --> 13:09.121
Are you not fishing today?

13:11.081 --> 13:13.292
-Well, I'm off so…
-You're off?

13:13.793 --> 13:15.419
Apparently, there are no clouds.

13:16.587 --> 13:18.631
There it is. There.

13:21.884 --> 13:24.345
You woke me up
to look at the sunrise?

13:24.845 --> 13:26.972
You know that condo
next to the restaurant?

13:27.473 --> 13:30.226
To see it from here,
you have to pay 30,000 won a night.

13:30.726 --> 13:32.978
You're getting to see it for free
just because of your dad.

13:33.062 --> 13:35.856
Oh, I can give you 30,000 won.

13:36.482 --> 13:37.316
Pay me, then.

13:40.653 --> 13:42.613
It feels wonderful to look at the sunrise.

13:43.280 --> 13:45.574
Oh, every time I see
the sun come up, I pray

13:46.325 --> 13:49.411
so that all things will go well
for you and your brother, Geum-myeong.

13:50.621 --> 13:52.832
You see the sunrise every morning?

13:52.915 --> 13:54.750
Are you out here so early every day?

13:57.920 --> 13:59.380
You don't ever want to sleep in?

13:59.463 --> 14:02.842
Oh, sure. I can't think of anybody
that doesn't wanna sleep in.

14:02.925 --> 14:05.886
So then why do you sail out
every morning this early?

14:08.848 --> 14:10.808
How can you live like this every day?

14:12.768 --> 14:14.186
Maybe if I sleep a little less,

14:15.062 --> 14:17.398
the two of you will get to sleep
a little more.

14:18.440 --> 14:21.527
That's why
I wake up so early, you see.

14:21.610 --> 14:23.028
If I think about it,

14:24.029 --> 14:27.199
there was never a day
when Dad woke up later than I did.

14:28.576 --> 14:30.035
Don't you have lotion?

14:30.119 --> 14:32.913
Wow, Mom only packed things you love.

14:33.664 --> 14:35.708
That's for you, Dad. It's rolled omelet.

14:35.791 --> 14:38.168
Your Mom was so excited
to prepare food for you.

14:40.254 --> 14:41.672
Does it ever get scary?

14:43.132 --> 14:44.133
Well, of course.

14:44.925 --> 14:47.845
There's nothing in the world
scarier than the ocean.

14:47.928 --> 14:51.515
So you just keep coming out here?
Even though you're scared?

14:52.308 --> 14:54.226
When the winds are strong, and I'm afraid,

14:55.019 --> 14:56.395
I always look at one thing.

14:56.478 --> 14:57.313
The lighthouse?

14:57.396 --> 14:58.564
Oh, no.

14:59.398 --> 15:01.650
Look. You see that small light over there?

15:03.110 --> 15:04.361
That's a fishing boat.

15:05.321 --> 15:06.780
The only beacon I need.

15:07.740 --> 15:11.619
See, if I believe people on that boat
are as lonely and scared as I am,

15:11.702 --> 15:12.620
it's less scary.

15:12.703 --> 15:14.622
It's less scary
knowing someone's with you here.

15:19.877 --> 15:22.463
Me and your mom
are never going to leave you,

15:23.255 --> 15:24.381
just like that boat.

15:25.758 --> 15:28.302
If ever you're hungry,
don't hesitate to come home.

15:30.471 --> 15:31.388
Dad, um,

15:33.140 --> 15:34.475
I need you to be honest.

15:35.351 --> 15:37.895
You're embarrassed in front of
all the neighbors because you

15:38.520 --> 15:40.105
already mailed the invitations.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.565
I'm not embarrassed.

15:41.649 --> 15:43.567
I would've been
if you'd married into that family.

15:44.735 --> 15:47.321
I knew things wouldn't work out
between you. I knew it.

15:47.404 --> 15:49.907
It'll work out, dear. I know it will.

15:50.866 --> 15:52.159
But you always say that.

15:53.452 --> 15:56.205
Just because you say it
doesn't mean it'll actually happen.

15:56.705 --> 15:57.873
What else can I do

15:59.124 --> 16:00.834
except to just wish you the best?

16:01.418 --> 16:04.630
If you were born into
a prosperous, successful house,

16:05.172 --> 16:07.132
they would've done everything for you,

16:08.300 --> 16:10.719
all kinds of things, and they'd make sure

16:10.803 --> 16:12.429
that you'd never get hurt.

16:12.930 --> 16:15.057
Then, in the next life, don't be my dad.

16:25.484 --> 16:27.319
Don't be my dad ever again.

16:27.945 --> 16:29.488
Save yourself the trouble.

16:29.571 --> 16:31.824
I'm glad to do it.

16:31.907 --> 16:33.117
I loved it.

16:33.200 --> 16:36.787
I never thought of it as trouble
because of you. No trouble at all.

16:36.870 --> 16:41.083
Dad, if you have 100 of something,
you always give me 120.

16:41.166 --> 16:42.918
Why do you keep doing that?

16:43.752 --> 16:45.754
Life wouldn't be easier with a rich dad.

16:46.463 --> 16:48.590
I wouldn't trade you
for Hyundai's founder.

16:51.301 --> 16:52.928
I think my knees are better now.

16:53.012 --> 16:55.848
Oh, please go to the hospital
if you're in pain.

16:55.931 --> 16:58.767
You think cooling patches
are going to solve the problem?

16:58.851 --> 17:00.394
This is so annoying.

17:01.895 --> 17:03.230
You're so annoying.

17:08.444 --> 17:10.654
I don't mind
if you're not marrying anyone.

17:12.364 --> 17:17.036
And if I'm being honest with you,
I… I think it's even better. I like it.

17:17.119 --> 17:18.328
I'll get hitched.

17:19.079 --> 17:20.956
You've always loved being married.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.042
Why tell me not to get married? Why?

17:49.777 --> 17:52.905
That day,
I saw the sun differently.

17:53.906 --> 17:55.741
It brought a new light

17:56.533 --> 17:58.160
over the lonely ocean.

17:59.578 --> 18:02.456
But it was only when
my own sun began setting

18:03.499 --> 18:08.045
that I realized how warm it was
to sit by my dad's side.

18:20.808 --> 18:21.934
Hey, there.

18:22.768 --> 18:24.019
Why were you on the boat?

18:24.812 --> 18:26.772
I watched the sun come up with Dad.

18:26.855 --> 18:29.024
Where's your mother? Is she not working?

18:29.525 --> 18:31.193
It was just me and my dad.

18:32.319 --> 18:33.695
-You two?
-Yes.

18:33.779 --> 18:35.447
-Just you two?
-Yes.

18:41.245 --> 18:42.871
Aren't you still in college or something?

18:42.955 --> 18:44.915
-Dad, do you need help?
-Nah.

18:44.998 --> 18:47.000
You look exactly like your mother did.

18:48.127 --> 18:49.128
Do you study hard?

18:49.211 --> 18:50.796
-I'm working, actually.
-Yeah? Where?

18:50.879 --> 18:52.965
-Major corporation.
-Which major corporation? Jeez.

18:56.760 --> 18:59.763
Ah, give it. It's Sunday.
You going out there?

18:59.847 --> 19:02.057
Why does it matter what day it is
to a fine sailor?

19:02.141 --> 19:04.393
Hey, put your shoes on properly.

19:05.269 --> 19:07.688
What? Your wife kicked you out again?

19:07.771 --> 19:09.940
Again? The hell do you know?

19:10.023 --> 19:11.817
What do you know about my family?

19:11.900 --> 19:13.944
Each family has a different dynamic, see?

19:14.027 --> 19:17.030
Why is he so rude to you, Dad?
He can't talk to you that way.

19:17.114 --> 19:21.160
Hey, your dad may be a captain now,
but you know what?

19:21.743 --> 19:25.497
He used to pull in the net,
cook noodles for me, and--

19:25.581 --> 19:29.418
Okay, that's really great.
However, you're both captains now.

19:29.501 --> 19:30.419
Yeah, you know we are.

19:32.004 --> 19:35.257
Eun-myeong broke up
with that man's daughter, right?

19:36.508 --> 19:39.178
That family. I'm telling you, man.
That family.

19:40.137 --> 19:41.263
Good God.

19:42.431 --> 19:44.600
Gwan-sik won't be working for you

19:45.434 --> 19:46.351
ever again.

19:48.312 --> 19:51.899
Okay, don't do it then. Just go away, man.
Just go home. Just leave now.

19:58.864 --> 20:01.533
Why would this spoiled brat hold his hand?
She's grown up.

20:02.034 --> 20:03.619
SANDGLASS

20:28.435 --> 20:29.394
So, uh,

20:30.270 --> 20:32.022
what are you up to these days?

20:32.105 --> 20:33.857
Are you doing okay at work?

20:38.278 --> 20:41.990
Selling makeup there, right?
Or did you sell your brain to the TV?

20:53.710 --> 20:54.544
So,

20:55.587 --> 20:58.548
uh, if you, uh, have time off some day,

20:59.383 --> 21:00.425
you wanna

21:01.468 --> 21:02.594
take a morning boat ride?

21:04.054 --> 21:04.888
Huh?

21:05.889 --> 21:06.723
You know, when

21:07.641 --> 21:08.892
the sun rises, and--

21:08.976 --> 21:10.143
Hire somebody.

21:10.811 --> 21:11.645
What?

21:12.271 --> 21:13.188
I'm busy too.

21:21.905 --> 21:24.366
You send that boy letters now? Huh?

21:25.325 --> 21:27.160
If you ever visit him, you're dead meat.

21:27.244 --> 21:29.496
-He won't see me even if I go.
-Say what?

21:31.456 --> 21:34.668
You went there, you sneaky little--
I'm sending that boy to a military prison.

21:35.460 --> 21:37.004
I have a friend who's a general.

21:43.343 --> 21:44.344
Wow.

21:46.096 --> 21:47.139
You are so shameless.

21:48.015 --> 21:48.932
Excuse me?

21:49.016 --> 21:51.685
You go around meeting women of all kinds.

21:51.768 --> 21:54.813
I think it's hilarious
that you tell me I can't see one guy.

21:54.896 --> 21:55.772
How dare you!

21:56.606 --> 21:58.275
You brat. What the hell do you know?

21:58.358 --> 22:01.361
All your kids saw the way you lived.
No one's taking you seriously.

22:01.862 --> 22:03.447
Just keep saying, "How dare you."

22:03.530 --> 22:05.782
Why you… I'm gonna shave
all your hair, you little--

22:05.866 --> 22:07.409
Fine, just shave my head.

22:08.160 --> 22:10.329
You've already ruined my life anyhow.

22:10.912 --> 22:12.873
Keep me here forever, then. I dare you.

22:18.503 --> 22:20.547
Don't be slamming that door on me, girl!

22:20.630 --> 22:22.049
It was the wind!

22:27.929 --> 22:29.097
-Honey.
-What?

22:29.181 --> 22:30.432
I'm too loud again?

22:30.515 --> 22:31.683
Did you buy this place?

22:32.267 --> 22:34.770
And tell me, what the hell
have you been studying?

22:35.854 --> 22:37.481
Uh, for dinner…

22:37.564 --> 22:38.815
Whatever you like.

22:39.399 --> 22:43.487
Actually, can you… go out for dinner?

22:43.987 --> 22:45.489
Why do you have to eat at home?

22:46.615 --> 22:47.866
It's a real bother.

22:51.078 --> 22:52.120
It's a real bother?

22:52.662 --> 22:54.206
It's a real bother?

22:55.082 --> 22:56.458
Why is it a bother?

22:57.084 --> 22:59.252
Put up your hands
if you think I'm a bother.

23:06.385 --> 23:07.386
T.O. I LOVE EUN-MYEONG

23:07.469 --> 23:09.513
WE'RE FAR YET CLOSE
I WILL ALWAYS WAIT FOR YOU

23:09.596 --> 23:11.431
I DO WAT I WANT
DON'T TELL ME WAT TO DO

23:14.643 --> 23:16.728
You all get to eat
because of me.

23:16.812 --> 23:17.896
Got it?

23:18.480 --> 23:19.856
Because of me!

23:24.820 --> 23:26.655
They have a kumquat field.

23:26.738 --> 23:29.741
It's two and a half acres, I think.
Or was it four acres?

23:30.242 --> 23:33.787
That's a pretty huge difference,
two and a half to four acres.

23:34.287 --> 23:37.207
Know what they say about
that family's dad? Have you heard?

23:37.290 --> 23:39.668
He's Seogwipo's Yang Gwan-sik, they say.

23:40.168 --> 23:41.711
He's a good husband.

23:42.754 --> 23:45.215
And they have more than a kumquat field.

23:45.715 --> 23:49.136
They own a mountain, and it's a huge one.

23:50.637 --> 23:52.431
And what, you've got a crush on that guy?

23:52.514 --> 23:54.683
Why are we talking about
the kumquat family?

23:54.766 --> 23:57.936
They have a kumquat field.
They own a mountain.

23:58.019 --> 24:00.897
They also have a son
who's a public official.

24:02.816 --> 24:05.777
He went to college in Seoul. He's 29.

24:07.612 --> 24:10.824
It's important to observe a man's father.

24:11.366 --> 24:13.994
He would've learned
how to treat his family from him.

24:14.077 --> 24:16.246
That why Eun-myeong's
such an expert at dating?

24:17.289 --> 24:19.666
The kumquat man's son
resembles Choi Jae-sung.

24:20.584 --> 24:22.002
You need a handsome man.

24:22.085 --> 24:25.130
You end up fighting less
if you marry a handsome one.

24:25.213 --> 24:28.341
Mom, it's been a year
since I broke off the engagement.

24:29.134 --> 24:31.553
So what? You did nothing wrong.

24:31.636 --> 24:33.472
Everyone in town knows we broke up, right?

24:33.555 --> 24:36.558
If I find someone new already,
how will that make me look?

24:38.727 --> 24:40.145
Who cares if they know?

24:43.732 --> 24:45.734
Not everybody in town knows about it.

24:54.784 --> 24:56.119
Why didn't you send these?

24:56.786 --> 24:57.996
Well, I…

24:59.498 --> 25:01.291
I knew you wouldn't follow through.

25:02.042 --> 25:03.168
What?

25:03.919 --> 25:05.837
That's how I raised you, dear.

25:14.012 --> 25:15.722
If she can't even
ride a tricycle,

25:15.805 --> 25:18.350
she'll just live in the kitchen
her whole life.

25:19.267 --> 25:21.436
I want Geum-myeong to really have it all,

25:21.520 --> 25:24.147
and I want her to really prosper
and to blossom.

25:24.231 --> 25:25.899
Geum-myeong should be thriving.

25:25.982 --> 25:29.194
I don't want her to set the table forever.

25:29.277 --> 25:31.530
I want her to flip the table over instead.

25:42.457 --> 25:45.126
Geum-myeong, go faster. Faster!

25:45.210 --> 25:46.378
Quick, quick, quick!

25:48.547 --> 25:50.382
Yes, go!

25:50.465 --> 25:51.758
Faster!

25:53.635 --> 25:56.555
Well,
why didn't you flip the table over?

25:57.055 --> 25:58.640
Did you not ever feel like it?

25:58.723 --> 26:00.225
Seven.

26:02.352 --> 26:03.728
Eight.

26:05.272 --> 26:07.399
Why did you have to be
the nice one all the time?

26:07.482 --> 26:09.442
It's not like there was a prize for it.

26:09.526 --> 26:11.236
ONE BASKET OF TANGERINES
80 WON FOR TEN

26:13.697 --> 26:15.240
That's 11.

26:17.200 --> 26:18.201
Huh?

26:18.285 --> 26:19.578
That's 11.

26:20.078 --> 26:21.496
Because of you.

26:21.580 --> 26:22.414
Oh.

26:23.290 --> 26:25.000
Because of you.

26:26.710 --> 26:31.256
You were looking at me
with those sweet, twinkling eyes.

26:31.965 --> 26:34.259
How could I not be aware of my actions?

26:38.763 --> 26:42.517
One thing I realized
after I gave birth to you and your brother

26:44.102 --> 26:46.688
is that the life I'm going to live then

26:46.771 --> 26:49.566
is one that you children would remember.

26:51.109 --> 26:53.361
You guys will talk about

26:54.529 --> 26:56.990
how I lived my life at the funeral.

26:58.366 --> 26:59.951
Once I realized that,

27:01.411 --> 27:04.164
I knew I had to be conscious
of my actions all the time.

27:07.417 --> 27:10.045
I realized
why the invitation said,

27:10.587 --> 27:14.341
"The Elder Daughter of
Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun."

27:15.425 --> 27:17.886
I was their Geum-myeong.

27:18.386 --> 27:19.387
Geum-myeong.

27:20.639 --> 27:22.807
You did absolutely nothing wrong.

27:23.433 --> 27:25.310
It's fortunate you avoided a pile of crap.

27:27.145 --> 27:29.397
Yeong-beom isn't crap, you know.

27:29.481 --> 27:31.900
I know. I know he isn't.

27:31.983 --> 27:34.319
You never have to tell me that. I know.

27:35.695 --> 27:37.280
I know you still cry inside.

27:40.241 --> 27:42.869
When you were a child,
you cried for four days

27:42.952 --> 27:45.830
when Kim Jeong-geun wouldn't sit with you.

27:49.167 --> 27:50.835
How do you remember his name?

27:51.419 --> 27:52.962
How can I forget it?

27:53.546 --> 27:56.299
My best friend
entrusted me with her secret.

28:09.312 --> 28:13.817
It's like boxing up your precious memories
and burying them underneath.

28:13.900 --> 28:14.984
Right?

28:15.068 --> 28:18.655
Sometimes, it's enjoyable to take it out
once in a while to look at.

28:20.699 --> 28:23.910
They always say first love
is for the memories, dear.

28:24.703 --> 28:26.621
Oh, Mom, what do you know?

28:26.705 --> 28:28.957
Your first love lives here with you.

28:30.583 --> 28:34.963
You need to enjoy life like you did
when you used to ride your tricycle.

28:35.046 --> 28:38.049
Not enjoying youth
is a massive waste, you know?

28:40.802 --> 28:42.387
My goodness.

28:42.887 --> 28:45.348
Your hands are still so soft.

28:49.310 --> 28:51.354
Just like fresh flower petals, dear.

28:51.438 --> 28:52.272
So new.

28:57.318 --> 28:58.737
Speak for yourself.

28:59.821 --> 29:01.614
Do something with your talent.

29:01.698 --> 29:02.824
Write your poems.

29:05.076 --> 29:06.953
I write every day.

29:07.036 --> 29:09.289
Over there is my poem collection.

29:10.623 --> 29:14.002
1995 HOUSEHOLD ACCOUNT BOOK
OH AE-SUN

29:15.962 --> 29:17.881
It was as though
I was a new outfit

29:17.964 --> 29:20.467
that had just been made
by a skillful tailor.

29:22.302 --> 29:24.763
When I left, I was in pieces,

29:24.846 --> 29:27.891
but when I returned,
I was stitched back together.

30:00.507 --> 30:01.966
She was only here a few days,

30:02.050 --> 30:05.220
but the house feels emptier than before.

30:08.014 --> 30:10.266
Well, it's just been
the two of us for a while now.

30:23.196 --> 30:24.823
Oh my goodness.

30:31.913 --> 30:34.457
She didn't have to do this. She didn't…

30:36.918 --> 30:38.628
She's so sweet.

30:39.128 --> 30:40.964
She's so sweet.

30:41.047 --> 30:43.049
FOR THE FOOD
WRITE YOUR POEM

30:44.300 --> 30:47.637
In our family,
receiving so much

30:47.720 --> 30:50.473
and repaying so little was acceptable,

30:50.557 --> 30:52.100
and unfairly so.

30:52.684 --> 30:54.269
Oh, my bones.

30:54.853 --> 30:56.980
My bones ache more and more every day.

31:03.152 --> 31:06.656
Being a mother
is a losing game, isn't it?

31:07.907 --> 31:12.537
Chung-su did haenyeo work
until after she was 80.

31:12.620 --> 31:15.415
They didn't find
one decent outfit for her coffin.

31:16.124 --> 31:19.544
All her children did was
to snatch money out of her hands.

31:20.169 --> 31:23.172
They were never bothered
that they took away her life's work.

31:23.256 --> 31:25.550
They blew all her money,
but they cried as if

31:25.633 --> 31:27.218
they were ever good to her.

31:27.302 --> 31:31.014
But still, she also said
that we witnessed a president

31:31.097 --> 31:32.891
who put on a prison uniform.

31:33.474 --> 31:38.021
At least she kept on working without
anyone's help until the end of her life.

31:38.104 --> 31:38.980
Oh God.

31:39.981 --> 31:42.734
A dog wouldn't even envy
a haenyeo's troubles.

31:43.234 --> 31:46.195
But it's not about adversity.
It's all about character.

31:46.988 --> 31:49.866
Ae-sun also needs
to draw the line somewhere.

31:49.949 --> 31:53.411
Everyone and their moms get cared for.
Of course she's always out of money.

31:53.494 --> 31:55.496
Should I try to stop her?

31:55.997 --> 31:56.998
Leave them alone.

31:57.081 --> 31:58.833
Once we leave this life,

31:58.917 --> 32:02.045
Ae-sun won't have any friends
or her aunts for that matter.

32:02.128 --> 32:05.381
We can't always defend her.
She must fend for herself for once.

32:09.469 --> 32:11.346
Uh…

32:13.014 --> 32:16.351
Well, at least I'm not gonna take it.
I hit back.

32:18.353 --> 32:21.731
Can't you be just a little nicer to folks?

32:22.565 --> 32:26.194
I guess I'm saying I don't get
why you have such good fortunes.

32:26.277 --> 32:28.321
My brother is a total fool for you.

32:28.905 --> 32:30.239
Your daughter is successful.

32:30.323 --> 32:33.284
These annoying haenyeo kind of
gave you this store for free.

32:33.368 --> 32:35.411
-Am I invisible?
-Know what else?

32:35.495 --> 32:38.790
I, your wonderful sister-in-law,
constantly take good care of your in-laws,

32:38.873 --> 32:41.250
-Don't I?
-I was wondering when you'd use that one.

32:41.334 --> 32:44.379
In principle, my brother's the eldest.
Why should I be caretaker?

32:44.462 --> 32:46.255
But you're not caretaker, are you?

32:46.339 --> 32:49.842
You had your parents sell their house
because of your business there.

32:49.926 --> 32:52.971
Now you're making your aging mom
take care of your kids.

32:53.054 --> 32:55.890
Who's the caretaker? Please, girl.

32:55.974 --> 32:57.600
That's my mom's most hated auntie.

32:57.684 --> 33:01.646
Listen, when you were a child,
Ae-sun fed you three square meals a day.

33:01.729 --> 33:04.649
You wouldn't be able to repay her
for what she did for you.

33:05.483 --> 33:08.569
-You think Ae-sun's money is your money?
-Why are you butting in?

33:08.653 --> 33:09.988
Hey!

33:10.071 --> 33:11.114
What is that?

33:11.656 --> 33:13.408
What did you bring this time?

33:16.035 --> 33:18.454
ELVAN WELLNESS MAT

33:25.336 --> 33:27.463
Ae-sun,
if Gwan-sik sleeps on that mat,

33:27.547 --> 33:30.133
his knee will be all better,
and he won't ever get cancer.

33:30.216 --> 33:32.218
You know I gave you a big discount, right?

33:32.301 --> 33:34.178
Couldn't take advantage like that.

33:34.262 --> 33:36.639
I think of you first
if I find anything special.

33:37.140 --> 33:41.394
If Gwan-sik places his finger on the mat
while it's warm, the infrared from it…

33:41.978 --> 33:45.106
Oh… What?
I can't give you a refund for that one.

33:46.858 --> 33:49.402
You said your mother's back
has been hurting a lot.

33:49.485 --> 33:51.779
Don't lie and say that
you bought it for her.

33:51.863 --> 33:54.157
Say that I'm the one who got it. Hmm?

33:54.240 --> 33:56.659
If I'm spending money,
I should get bragging rights.

33:57.994 --> 34:00.663
You want
to embarrass me with this.

34:00.747 --> 34:01.748
Go.

34:02.832 --> 34:04.000
Go.

34:04.876 --> 34:08.463
Hey. Please don't bring anything
to sell next time, okay?

34:10.048 --> 34:11.424
Ae-sun.

34:12.175 --> 34:13.968
Character molds destiny, right?

34:15.386 --> 34:18.389
What, you envy my good fortunes now, huh?

34:19.057 --> 34:19.891
Well…

34:21.768 --> 34:24.520
Look. You took all my cash again today.

34:29.317 --> 34:30.485
Come eat another one.

34:31.110 --> 34:32.487
One more bite. One more.

34:34.655 --> 34:37.116
Oh, why do I deserve pain like this?

34:37.867 --> 34:41.746
Who knew that I'd still be babysitting
my grandkids at this age?

34:42.580 --> 34:45.291
When you're done,
can you unplug these? Prevents fires.

34:45.374 --> 34:47.543
Gyeong-ok blames me
for not dressing her kids

34:47.627 --> 34:49.504
with enough clothes
whenever they get sick.

34:49.587 --> 34:52.131
This is worse than taking care of
your dad's parents.

34:52.632 --> 34:55.426
-Ya!
-Seo Dong-min, stand guard.

34:55.510 --> 34:58.221
Attention! Atten-hut! Atten-hut!

34:59.138 --> 34:59.972
Oh God.

35:00.640 --> 35:03.434
Why come here if you're just gonna
sit around without making a sound?

35:03.518 --> 35:06.270
Go. Go home. Go to your wife.

35:06.354 --> 35:08.356
No one's been on my side my whole life.

35:09.899 --> 35:11.818
Your back. How is it?

35:12.693 --> 35:14.320
Please worry about your wife's back.

35:14.403 --> 35:16.739
Well, inflammation patches
won't be enough.

35:16.823 --> 35:19.325
You need to get acupuncture.

35:19.992 --> 35:21.410
I'll take you for treatment.

35:21.911 --> 35:24.789
I must say I was probably
on Ae-sun's side a lot.

35:24.872 --> 35:27.875
No one on this planet
would be so loyal to one's wife

35:27.959 --> 35:30.086
against his mom as often as you.

35:30.920 --> 35:31.754
Listen.

35:32.672 --> 35:34.841
I wouldn't trade you
for Hyundai's founder.

35:36.217 --> 35:39.262
I wouldn't trade you if Shin Saimdang
was available for a mother.

35:39.345 --> 35:40.638
Hey. Pick your foot up.

35:40.721 --> 35:42.598
Why would Shin Saimdang
wanna be your mother?

35:42.682 --> 35:44.559
She's got a preference too, I'm sure.

35:45.768 --> 35:47.812
I won't count on you
or your wife to treat me better.

35:47.895 --> 35:51.190
There is no mother that can take pride in
having a fool for a son.

35:51.274 --> 35:53.526
Even Shin Saimdang would turn her back.

35:56.487 --> 35:57.321
Here, here.

35:58.865 --> 36:01.200
If your disrespectful son is here,

36:01.701 --> 36:03.369
you should make him clean.

36:03.452 --> 36:05.079
Who implied that son? Who?

36:06.122 --> 36:08.541
-Who said that?
-You said dogs are better, remember?

36:09.125 --> 36:10.376
Everyone in town knows that.

36:10.960 --> 36:12.587
Tell them to quit talking crap.

36:12.670 --> 36:14.213
You've done good things.

36:18.342 --> 36:19.969
I don't know anything about
losing a child,

36:20.052 --> 36:21.762
but I know what it's like to lose parents.

36:24.015 --> 36:26.100
Watching you move on was honorable enough.

36:26.684 --> 36:28.603
Everybody knows about that.

36:47.705 --> 36:49.498
Mom. Hey.

36:49.999 --> 36:53.336
It's Jong-gu. Jong-gu.
Your eldest grandson Jong-gu is here.

36:54.003 --> 36:56.422
Grandma, it's Jong-gu. Remember me?

36:57.673 --> 36:59.884
You don't recognize him, Mom?

36:59.967 --> 37:02.261
Jong-gu, the pathetic, dull dimwit.

37:03.012 --> 37:05.181
Mom, you taught Jong-gu how to write.

37:05.264 --> 37:09.518
He didn't know how to multiply,
but now he's a card shark, you know?

37:12.021 --> 37:14.315
Chun-ok, you know who I am? Huh?

37:14.398 --> 37:15.358
Who am I?

37:15.441 --> 37:16.734
Chun-ok. Hey.

37:20.112 --> 37:21.530
Oh my.

37:21.614 --> 37:24.533
Mom, you used to be so well-versed
in writing when you were younger.

37:24.617 --> 37:26.202
Now your mind is fading.

37:26.285 --> 37:29.163
Why is it that your mind
has left you already?

37:29.872 --> 37:30.706
Oh, hello.

37:31.540 --> 37:32.959
Hi, Ae-sun.

37:33.042 --> 37:34.126
Come on. Come on in.

37:34.210 --> 37:35.628
When did you come down?

37:35.711 --> 37:38.756
I thought maybe I might never celebrate
my sister's birthday again.

37:38.839 --> 37:41.008
I'm afraid this might be her last.

37:43.052 --> 37:44.136
Grandma.

37:44.637 --> 37:45.930
It's me. Ae-sun.

37:46.555 --> 37:49.433
She doesn't know.
She's forgotten everyone.

37:50.101 --> 37:53.729
Ae-sun, I'm really, really upset.

37:53.813 --> 37:55.189
She doesn't remember me.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.149
Goodness.

37:58.359 --> 37:59.610
Grandma.

38:00.319 --> 38:01.153
Oh.

38:02.863 --> 38:05.783
Grandma, I brought
senbei crackers for you. Senbei. Huh?

38:06.701 --> 38:10.204
-After you finish up your meal, you can--
-I remember.

38:17.545 --> 38:19.422
Han-gyu's daughter.

38:23.342 --> 38:25.011
My Han-gyu's daughter.

38:33.978 --> 38:34.812
So,

38:36.105 --> 38:37.982
have you been well?

39:02.590 --> 39:04.300
Grandma, I guess I've been

39:04.925 --> 39:06.969
Han-gyu's daughter to you all along.

39:09.764 --> 39:12.850
You always forget my name,
but not that I'm Han-gyu's daughter.

39:13.351 --> 39:16.228
Does that make you upset?

39:16.896 --> 39:18.522
I love it.

39:20.149 --> 39:22.693
I really appreciate it.

39:22.777 --> 39:24.028
What?

39:24.987 --> 39:26.280
What is the matter?

39:27.114 --> 39:28.032
What is it?

39:28.115 --> 39:29.909
What's bothering you?

39:31.077 --> 39:31.994
What is it?

39:32.078 --> 39:33.788
Child, what is the matter?

39:34.538 --> 39:36.540
Child, what is the matter?

39:36.624 --> 39:37.917
Nothing's the matter.

39:38.000 --> 39:39.460
It's nothing at all.

39:41.087 --> 39:43.672
If something were wrong,
you'd buy her a new boat.

39:44.298 --> 39:47.802
When Han-gyu's daughter said
she was having a hard time,

39:47.885 --> 39:50.221
you bought her a whole new boat.

39:50.721 --> 39:52.681
Mother, I'm struggling too.

39:53.599 --> 39:56.143
Your 60-year-old daughter-in-law
is also suffering.

39:56.227 --> 39:58.104
So will you get me a boat as well?

39:58.187 --> 39:59.313
Stop it.

40:02.024 --> 40:04.235
Grandma, listen,

40:05.027 --> 40:07.363
would you like to… to live with us?

40:07.446 --> 40:08.280
Oh, no.

40:08.906 --> 40:10.658
But you should come live with us.

40:11.158 --> 40:12.159
No.

40:13.077 --> 40:15.704
You know Gwan-sik is a good man.

40:15.788 --> 40:18.332
He'll do anything I ask of him.

40:19.375 --> 40:20.209
I said no.

40:20.292 --> 40:21.210
Why not?

40:21.794 --> 40:23.379
Not your home, darling.

40:26.048 --> 40:27.508
Am I a stranger to you?

40:27.591 --> 40:29.510
Is that really what you think, huh?

40:33.472 --> 40:37.101
Grandma, how about I get you new dentures?

40:37.768 --> 40:38.894
How's that sound?

40:39.854 --> 40:42.982
I'm just going to pull money
out of my savings

40:43.065 --> 40:45.568
and then get you some nice dentures.

40:46.402 --> 40:49.113
You'll get dentures?

40:49.196 --> 40:50.448
Mm-hmm.

40:50.531 --> 40:52.324
You helped me back then

40:52.408 --> 40:55.828
when I needed some new teeth
when I was a child, remember?

40:56.328 --> 40:58.706
♪ Leopard cub with no teeth ♪

40:58.789 --> 41:01.250
♪ Don't go near the water now ♪

41:01.333 --> 41:03.669
♪ You will scare the baby fish ♪

41:03.752 --> 41:05.963
♪ Don't go near the magpie ♪

41:06.046 --> 41:07.840
♪ Caw, caw, they will hide ♪

41:07.923 --> 41:10.676
Let's see. Let's see.
I'm not pulling the tooth.

41:10.759 --> 41:13.137
I just wanna see if I did it right.

41:13.220 --> 41:16.223
Don't lie to me.
You're gonna pull it out, aren't you?

41:17.850 --> 41:20.227
You're so smart,
just like your dad. Silly girl.

41:20.311 --> 41:22.688
Let's pull that tooth.
That crow is waiting for your tooth.

41:22.771 --> 41:25.191
Wait a bit. Wait a bit.
Just let me count to ten.

41:25.274 --> 41:28.444
It's not bad. It doesn't hurt at all.

41:28.527 --> 41:31.238
Pull his tooth first.
His tooth is loose too.

41:31.739 --> 41:33.157
So I'm sure if it's painful or not.

41:33.240 --> 41:36.076
Oh, his parents can pull his tooth out.

41:40.206 --> 41:42.875
Why do you have a string
wrapped around your tooth?

41:42.958 --> 41:44.835
Go and ask your family to do it.

41:44.919 --> 41:46.420
You're here to sell hairtail.

41:46.504 --> 41:48.631
Why are you getting
your tooth pulled here?

41:48.714 --> 41:51.842
Gwan-sik, you do it first.

41:51.926 --> 41:53.219
Can you please be first?

41:54.803 --> 41:57.640
Can you see if it's painful, please?

42:00.768 --> 42:01.852
Aren't you scared?

42:02.978 --> 42:04.271
So you're ready to do it?

42:07.691 --> 42:10.152
Oh, my girl. You're so intelligent.

42:10.736 --> 42:13.197
Where did you find a silly guy like him?

42:14.073 --> 42:15.658
Good work. Good work.

42:17.159 --> 42:18.494
Hmm?

42:18.577 --> 42:20.955
-Did you pull it?
-Feel anything?

42:23.249 --> 42:26.585
Eventually,
we lose our teeth for the second time.

42:28.879 --> 42:31.090
I can't believe that the little child

42:31.173 --> 42:34.552
without her front teeth
grew up to be so big.

42:34.635 --> 42:36.845
The old black crows

42:36.929 --> 42:39.390
won't bring you
a new tooth now, will they?

42:40.391 --> 42:42.017
Let me take care of your teeth.

42:43.435 --> 42:45.896
Something is the matter, my child.

42:49.817 --> 42:51.527
I know how you feel.

42:52.653 --> 42:54.738
I know exactly how you feel.

42:56.657 --> 42:58.033
There are times

42:58.117 --> 43:01.829
when I want to call out his name
at the top of my lungs…

43:04.373 --> 43:06.500
and cry my heart out.

43:09.044 --> 43:10.546
After holding it in

43:11.130 --> 43:13.090
for all of my life,

43:14.383 --> 43:16.802
saying Han-gyu's name is…

43:19.763 --> 43:22.182
even more difficult to utter than ever.

43:25.519 --> 43:27.438
And I feel terrible that I can't.

43:33.569 --> 43:34.862
So I know

43:36.113 --> 43:37.448
how you feel.

43:39.491 --> 43:41.785
I know exactly how you feel.

44:16.028 --> 44:18.030
I know how you feel.

44:19.490 --> 44:20.908
Hearing her words,

44:21.450 --> 44:24.119
Mom laid her head on her grandmother's lap

44:27.039 --> 44:29.708
and cried her heart out for a long time.

44:34.463 --> 44:36.173
Why won't you go with her?

44:36.256 --> 44:38.801
She's your favorite son,
Han-gyu's daughter.

44:38.884 --> 44:41.720
Oh, I really wonder how much this cost.

44:42.721 --> 44:45.683
What? Are you uncomfortable with her?

44:45.766 --> 44:47.351
Her husband and her?

44:47.434 --> 44:49.687
This is expensive, isn't it?

44:49.770 --> 44:52.648
Hey, you bought her a boat,
so why feel bad about this?

44:52.731 --> 44:55.025
Nothing wrong with your granddaughter
buying you this.

44:57.903 --> 45:00.114
I didn't do that much for her.

45:00.948 --> 45:03.242
I never even gave her any croaker.

45:04.118 --> 45:05.619
How can I live there?

45:05.703 --> 45:08.122
Shit, nobody forgets those damn croakers.

45:08.706 --> 45:11.542
You poured all of
your life savings into her, didn't you?

45:12.543 --> 45:13.377
Oh.

45:14.294 --> 45:15.879
In the hereafter…

45:17.881 --> 45:20.676
all I'll hear is Han-gyu screaming at me.

45:22.386 --> 45:24.096
All I'll get to hear

45:24.179 --> 45:26.765
is my son screaming at me.

45:38.110 --> 45:39.778
It's warm. Oh.

45:43.741 --> 45:45.909
I think I'll sleep well tonight.

46:10.142 --> 46:12.227
Oh, look. Mama.

46:12.895 --> 46:14.480
It's as if you're a newlywed.

46:15.564 --> 46:17.983
Your children will remember you
by this photo.

46:18.776 --> 46:20.694
Pink is a good color for you.

46:21.695 --> 46:23.739
Did I do well, my dear?

46:26.033 --> 46:28.118
Have I paid off your debt?

46:31.121 --> 46:32.664
Yes, truly. Of course.

46:33.916 --> 46:35.250
You did so well.

46:37.503 --> 46:39.922
Oh, I'm running out of breath.

46:40.631 --> 46:43.050
I think I'm just about ready.

46:46.804 --> 46:49.056
You may breathe your last one now.

46:51.725 --> 46:52.810
So,

46:53.560 --> 46:54.394
was it

46:55.270 --> 46:58.982
a wonderful life or… or a hard one?

47:12.287 --> 47:14.623
It was a wonderful life.

47:15.123 --> 47:17.709
I got to live a life with all my children.

47:19.294 --> 47:22.422
It was an amazing life.

47:36.436 --> 47:37.855
I can't believe it.

47:37.938 --> 47:40.691
KIM CHUN-OK OF GIMHAE KIM CLAN
MAY YOU FINALLY BE REUNITED

47:40.774 --> 47:44.236
Now we say goodbye
to someone every season.

47:45.529 --> 47:46.363
Right?

47:49.741 --> 47:51.285
We don't know what we had

47:51.368 --> 47:53.829
until they're gone, one after another.

47:55.122 --> 47:57.082
Both my parents.

47:58.584 --> 48:00.836
Your grandmother, your father.

48:12.764 --> 48:13.932
You're right, Mother.

48:15.392 --> 48:18.312
My son's wife was definitely
a cut above your son's wife.

48:19.730 --> 48:20.564
Yeah.

48:26.028 --> 48:26.862
Oh.

48:27.487 --> 48:28.822
I did it again.

48:28.906 --> 48:30.574
I brought three spoons.

48:32.576 --> 48:34.536
Auntie Chung-su.

48:38.707 --> 48:39.917
My grandmother.

48:41.835 --> 48:45.589
You really should've gotten… dentures.

48:47.341 --> 48:48.508
And…

49:00.354 --> 49:01.355
I hope you and I

49:03.106 --> 49:04.274
leave this life together.

49:07.527 --> 49:08.362
Hmm?

49:19.081 --> 49:21.667
We think
we arrive at the picnic together,

49:22.376 --> 49:24.836
but people all leave at different times.

49:25.837 --> 49:27.923
Just as the tides ebb and flow,

49:29.341 --> 49:30.801
some leave us,

49:32.469 --> 49:33.428
but some…

49:35.013 --> 49:36.807
Oh, he's here.

49:36.890 --> 49:38.850
The door's open. It's open.

49:38.934 --> 49:40.435
…return to us.

49:41.395 --> 49:46.149
Oh!
Oh, dear. I'm so, so happy you're back.

49:46.233 --> 49:48.986
Oh, Eun-myeong. It is so nice to see you.

49:49.069 --> 49:50.737
Thanks so much, son.

49:52.447 --> 49:55.867
Oh, well, why are you just standing there?
Get in here.

49:55.951 --> 49:58.453
I made all kinds of things for you.

49:58.537 --> 50:01.123
What is it? You wanna salute us?

50:02.874 --> 50:04.960
Salute?

50:05.544 --> 50:08.505
Hang on. Why do you have so much luggage?

50:15.345 --> 50:16.179
Mother.

50:16.263 --> 50:17.806
Okay. Go. Go ahead.

50:23.770 --> 50:25.897
What, you bring something?

50:26.606 --> 50:27.649
What?

50:30.569 --> 50:32.112
Hi. It's been a while.

50:32.946 --> 50:34.406
Oh my.

50:38.618 --> 50:40.037
Hi, Hyeon-suk.

50:41.079 --> 50:42.247
Bu Hyeon-suk, right?

50:46.960 --> 50:49.171
Oh my. Oh, you… you guys

50:50.088 --> 50:53.508
are still… still together. Wow.

50:53.592 --> 50:56.261
So what's this about?

51:03.143 --> 51:04.186
Uh…

51:05.020 --> 51:07.481
Wh… why do you have
your hand on your b… belly?

51:07.564 --> 51:10.108
Oh, oh, please don't scare me like that,
Hyeon-suk. What?

51:10.192 --> 51:13.278
-Mother, Father.
-What? What? What? What?

51:13.361 --> 51:15.864
No. Aah! I… I don't want to hear this.

51:15.947 --> 51:17.324
You're Grandma and Grandpa.

51:19.159 --> 51:20.410
Oh my God.

51:24.790 --> 51:26.291
You're Han-bang's grandmother.

51:27.417 --> 51:29.586
In spite of
the coldest weather,

51:29.669 --> 51:32.089
new buds always fight their way
out of the ground.

51:32.714 --> 51:35.217
-You idiotic, shameful… where is it?
-Just like their springtime…

51:35.300 --> 51:37.677
-Oh.
-…their winter arrived too soon.

51:37.761 --> 51:39.513
Where is it? You idiot.

51:39.596 --> 51:41.640
You were supposed to serve your country.

52:27.561 --> 52:28.603
Huh?

52:29.938 --> 52:30.897
Stop!

53:07.893 --> 53:09.644
Geum-myeong, wait!

53:22.032 --> 53:23.700
Yang Geum-myeong!

53:25.285 --> 53:26.578
Yang Geum-myeong!

53:31.958 --> 53:34.002
Geum-myeong!

53:35.587 --> 53:39.007
A winter
as sparkly as their spring

53:39.799 --> 53:40.967
was on its way.

53:44.304 --> 53:47.057
A GLISTENING WINTER

56:33.556 --> 56:38.895
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."
